hi i'm here in kaiapoi  behind me is the kaiapoi river  i'd like to talk to you about the  government's three waters reform  you'll have seen that there's been a lot  of material starting to be out in the  media and even in our local  newspapers we have been putting some  articles as a council there to explain  the position  i'm disappointed with the government's  advertising campaign  it presents a very misleading position  that we have sludge coming out of our  shower taps that is not correct  and it's inappropriate that that's how  this campaign is being uh put together  we're proud of what we've done as a  council  over the last 20 years we've invested  over 100 million dollars  making sure that you have safe  drinking water and also that we're  dealing with things responsibly like our  sewage  and our storm water  this coming week the council uh going  out to you with a  a letter and a pamphlet and a feedback  form  we want to know what your thoughts are  on the three waters reform  because at the end of the day you own  the assets and it's important for us to  know what your position is on it  our council is required by the  government to come back with a position  by the end of september  we're asking that you get your  information your feedback to us  following receiving the information by  the 5th of september we're going to hold  seven drop-in sessions that the  councillors  and myself will be attending and we  welcome your attendance you can also  give us your feedback on  waimakariri.govt.nz let's talk we'll be  in touch if there's any questions you  have  to us it's really important that we  receive your feedback before we make our  decision known to the government by the  end of september so please let us know  what you're thinking  thank you and we look forward to  receiving your feedback
 

